{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on the published-failure intent seam (question f1ec0916),\n28 October 2026. Ruling ed818781 stands in full; it reads stale only\nbecause its base eb1ed32c was retired after it was answered. This\nruling rests on the slice request a53e1464 and on the question.\n\n1. \"For the maintainers\" in the design's stage table means the members\n   who may triage: the bounded active holders of issue.triage, read\n   through the existing holders observation ({ of, holders, most }).\n   That is the operational reading, approved. In the first role table\n   those holders are exactly the admin and maintainer roles, and when a\n   room grants issue.triage to other roles they are the maintainers for\n   this purpose. No literal role-roster observation is authorized and\n   none is needed. In data and UI call them the triagers.\n\n2. Genesis: approved as proposed. The incident issue is declared as a\n   nested successor of the Change that landed, created through the\n   existing Directory-rooted create closure and numbered by the existing\n   index row. No new Directory handler. Its origin is the system, bound\n   to the recorded facts: the sibling Destination, the admitted\n   published job, the publication, and the native failure decision. No\n   MemberRef requester is fabricated and no automatic signing key is\n   introduced. Ordinary edit-own then grants nobody special authority.\n\n3. Bounds: one incident state per job; a retry re-sends only the\n   original pending envelope; an unknown creation never starts a\n   replacement; failure and hold state stay Destination-owned and\n   atomic. When the triagers are unknown, empty or over the observation\n   bound, the incident is retained in a visible pending or refused\n   state and neither the failure nor the hold is dropped. Approved.\n\n4. The slice head updates the design note: the stage table row and the\n   sentence after it say the intent goes to the holders of issue.triage,\n   and the disposition names this ruling. The prep note 0ff2027f is the\n   builder's working record; the PD-2 note of the head carries what the\n   checker needs.\n\nThis is the commissioned published-failure exchange of the first slice.\nThe marking-time proof exchange stays excluded as ed818781 said.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f1ec0916f786c9a755dbbfca92b9696b9790da07 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:eb1ed32cf631cc680a9371662fe1d45d0f2f26e0","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}